\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{3}{An illustration of the architecture of GAT-PCM with a small DCOP instance. A DCOP instance in (a) is first transformed into an equivalent microstructure $G$ in (b), and then $G$ is instantiated with a partial assignment $\Gamma $ by removing some nodes and edges in (c) and then further compiled to a directed tripartite graph with a given target assignment in (d) (cf. the section ``Graph Representations'' for details) in (e). Finally, we use GATs to learn an embedding with supervised training (cf. the sections ``Graph Embeddings" and ``Pretraining" for details).}{}{}}
